{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017H9EuC6Lkk47tsei1XFHt2","type":"tool_result","content":"1027 PLAN.md\n1:# Gauntletdown\n18:## Contents\n36:## 0. Read this first\n50:## 1. The game on one page\n59:### What makes Gauntlet distinctive, and how this game captures it\n76:### Originality guardrails (non-negotiable)\n85:## 2. Deliverables and folder layout\n87:### The run folder (this folder)\n96:### The dev subfolder\n120:### What the finished demo contains\n126:## 3. Architecture\n128:### 3.1 Base\n134:### 3.2 Modules (`game/src/`, concatenated in name order inside one IIFE)\n171:### 3.3 Runtime model: simulation, intents, view, network\n192:### 3.4 Scenes and flow\n205:### 3.5 Engine changes (the engine is ours to change; keep each one small and tested)\n222:### 3.6 Build and bundle (`build.mjs`)\n253:## 4. Systems and mechanics (the spec)\n257:### 4.1 Floors, the map and the legend\n291:### 4.2 Heroes\n319:### 4.3 Controls and prompts (10-foot, controller-first)\n343:### 4.4 Combat and damage\n351:### 4.5 Monsters\n372:### 4.6 Generators\n379:### 4.7 Items\n404:### 4.8 Level features\n422:### 4.9 Floor flow\n430:### 4.10 Death, rising again, continue, game over, high scores\n437:### 4.11 Scoring\n441:### 4.12 The narrator: \"The Gaunt\"\n448:### 4.13 Camera and local co-op\n458:### 4.14 HUD (canvas pixel art, anchored to `r.W`/`r.H`, clear of `game.cornerArea()`)\n468:### 4.15 Front-end screens (canvas pixel art; big; mouse, keys and controller)\n479:### 4.16 Pause menu and Settings\n484:### 4.17 Dev Tools (from the pause menu; not in sessions, not in attract)\n495:### 4.18 Attract mode and the autopilot\n503:### 4.19 Touch-only devices\n510:### 4.20 Online: AI Hub sessions (shared world) and the game on its own\n548:### 4.21 Audio (all synthesized in code; no audio files)\n582:### 4.22 Art direction\n608:### 4.23 Animation\n627:### 4.24 Difficulty, scaling and the tuning table\n654:## 5. Content\n656:### 5.1 Story and story b