{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrdwHzP5qcG5BXSb93W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the draw and input API. A few more specifics to pin down before writing: player movement and aim accessors, TileMap spawn lookup, and how the kits trigger melee swings."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3059,"cache_read_input_tokens":126652,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3059},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"1d35add5-0a90-47e7-bb21-eeea201a18b5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:48.702Z","request_id":"req_011CghrdvwAaH6Je4bfJZVda"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrdwHzP5qcG5BXSb93W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LzWxLxAokQTd5vAArrLjw5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n '^- `input\\.\\(move\\|padAim\\|aimSource\\|pointer\\|lastDevice\\|label\\|pressed\\|down\\|clicked\\|consume\\)\\|^- `game.mouseGround\\|^- `map.find\\|^- `map.findAll\\|^- `map.solid\\|^- `game.setView\\|^- `game.after\\|^- `game.cam\\b\\|^- `game.cam.frame\\|^- `game.follow\\|^- `game.flash\\|^- `game.hitFx\\|^- `game.shake\\|^- `game.go(' API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300; echo ....; grep -n 'swing\\s*=\\|E.move(' kits/adventure.js | head -5 | cut -c1-240; echo ...; grep -n 'findAll\\|find(' API-INDEX.md | head -5 | cut -c1-200","description":"Grep API for input accessors, map finders, camera and swing helpers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3059,"cache_read_input_tokens":126652,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3059},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"26efda08-3490-4f0f-abb0-cfa24b9fb1e8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:50.729Z","request_id":"req_011CghrdvwAaH6Je4bfJZVda","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LzWxLxAokQTd5vAArrLjw5":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050253__x8ffc89/work/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253 && grep -n '^- `input\\.\\(move\\|padAim\\|aimSource\\|pointer\\|lastDevice\\|label\\|pressed\\|down\\|clicked\\|consume\\)\\|^- `game.mouseGround\\|^- `map.find\\|^- `map.findAll\\|^- `map.solid\\|^- `game.setView\\|^- `game.after\\|^- `game.cam\\b\\|^- `game.cam.frame\\|^- `game.follow\\|^- `game.flash\\|^- `game.hitFx\\|^- `game.shake\\|^- `game.go(' API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300; echo ....; grep -n 'swing\\s*=\\|E.move(' kits/adventure.js | head -5 | cut -c1-240; echo ...; grep -n 'findAll\\|find(' API-INDEX.md | head -5 | cut -c1-200","description":"Grep API for input accessors, map finders, camera and swing helpers"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01LzWxLxAokQTd5vAArrLjw5":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050253__x8ffc89/work/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LzWxLxAokQTd5vAArrLjw5","type":"tool_result","content":"282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(inpu\n284:- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n285:- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n287:- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n296:- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n301:- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n323:- `input.aimSource = 'move'` †: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad'\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n334:- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n470:- `game.after(seconds, fn)`: run fn once after `seconds` of game time. Cleared on scene change. Returns { cancel() }\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n480:- `game.follow(target, o = {})`: keep the camera on an object automatically (instead of calling focus every update). opts: { z: extra height to look at (default 16), lead: look ahead in the facing / moving direction }. follow(null) stops.\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris', 'mosaic', 'swirl' or 'dissolve', each way taking \n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n499:- `game.shake(a)`: shake the screen by a (pixels, decaying; at most 10 in all); none when reduceMotion, scaled by the player's settings.shake\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the ca\n750:- `map.find(tag)`: first spawn with this tag ({ x, y, z, cx, cy }), or null\n751:- `map.findAll(tag)`: every spawn with this tag\n767:- `map.solid(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: make a shape solid in this map: map.solid(id | entry, x, y, z, o) with r.shape's placement (facing, scale, flip, params) -> the solid ({ x, y (the footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy, c, s, shape, px, py (where it was placed) }; map.solids holds them; wh\n768:- `map.solidAt(x, y)`: solidCell at a world point\n769:- `map.solidCell(cx, cy)`: true where a cell has a wall (or is outside the map); walkable() also counts blocked floor\n....\n120:      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n539:        f.aim = !c.busy && f.t < .6 && E.move('cast', Math.max(0, f.t / .6), 'recover');\n...\n750:- `map.find(tag)`: first spawn with this tag ({ x, y, z, cx, cy }), or null\n751:- `map.findAll(tag)`: every spawn with this tag\n854:- `level.find(tag)`: the first spawn with this tag ({ x, y: 0, z, cx, cz }), or null\n855:- `level.findAll(tag)`: every spawn with this tag\n1640:- `E.Songbook`: the songbook: songs by id, their moods, get(id), find(mood) (see the manual)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"18ca1213-c4db-41f6-af4d-d030dd0b49d2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:50.755Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(inpu\n284:- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n285:- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n287:- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n296:- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n301:- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n323:- `input.aimSource = 'move'` †: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad'\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n334:- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n470:- `game.after(seconds, fn)`: run fn once after `seconds` of game time. Cleared on scene change. Returns { cancel() }\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n480:- `game.follow(target, o = {})`: keep the camera on an object automatically (instead of calling focus every update). opts: { z: extra height to look at (default 16), lead: look ahead in the facing / moving direction }. follow(null) stops.\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris', 'mosaic', 'swirl' or 'dissolve', each way taking \n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n499:- `game.shake(a)`: shake the screen by a (pixels, decaying; at most 10 in all); none when reduceMotion, scaled by the player's settings.shake\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. 