{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghsu1wa3kgkaXmJj7eJB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Dev Tools page fits now. Next are the deliverable's remaining parts: the About screen's feedback text, `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` (no engine changes were made), and `exit-interview.json`. The About screen and the JSON must carry the same answers, so I'll write them once, in matching form."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2785,"cache_read_input_tokens":328405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2785},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"dda58e73-4583-4182-a42d-3fd0cd9a8437","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:21:45.594Z","request_id":"req_011Cghsu1cV5DtKPQp95a1SA"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghsu1wa3kgkaXmJj7eJB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YbXM44jPShLi8YiGH5YmBT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > game/src/80-about.js <<'EOF'\n// About and credits: the pages on the About screen. The Source Information and the feedback sections are the same text\n// as the chat reply and exit-interview.json. Each paragraph is wrapped to the screen when the game loads.\nconst ABOUT_TEXT = [\n  ['CREDITS', [\n    'GAUNTLETDOWN, VERSION 0.1. Built by Claude Haiku 5.5, medium effort, from PLAN.md and TASK.md.',\n    'Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 by Michael Crosato (MIT), handoff folder, unmodified.',\n    'Generic props from the engine asset store: Kenney and KayKit, CC0.',\n    'Inspired by Gauntlet, Atari Games, 1985. An original homage: no names, art, music or lines from that game are used here.',\n    'Music, sound and voice are generated in code. No audio files.',\n    'THE GAUNT IS NOT DEAD. IT IS ONLY DIGESTING.'\n  ]],\n  ['SOURCE INFORMATION', [\n    'Date: 2026-11-04 05:02:53. Source: Gauntlet, Atari Games, 1985 arcade. Plan: PLAN.md.',\n    'Genre: arcade co-op dungeon crawler, top-down hack-and-shoot. Perspective: three-quarter overhead, with top-down and isometric in Settings.',\n    'Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 on Canvas 2D and Web Audio; tests on Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0.',\n    'Art: the engine look, procedural rigs, textured floors and walls, canvas lighting, pixel sprites. One realm, The Larder, in this build.',\n    'Animation: engine rigs and E.MOVES attacks (overhead swing, throw). Monsters and generators bob and flash.',\n    'Audio: engine chip songs and sound presets. No voices or original music in this build.',\n    'Online: none. Testing: 43 headless checks, a scripted playthrough run twice, the engine browser checker. Research: engine docs and source; no web research.',\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; Chromium for the checks. Model: Anthropic claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium. Usage: unknown.'\n  ]],\n  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\n    'Issues caught: about 13. Four were game-breaking: the Escape key could not open the pause menu, the pause overlay crashed on Resume, the last stairs crashed into a missing floor, and a second run would never show its game over.',\n    'Most helpful test: the scripted playthrough from title to ending, through every scene, run twice.',\n    'Least helpful test: the screenshot look notes, which flagged the flat colours of a dungeon.'\n  ]],\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\n    'Liked most: the TileMap, Humanoid rigs, FlowField and Bullets do the hard parts, and headless advance and input make a whole playthrough run in seconds.',\n    'Stuck or guessed wrong: yes. Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, so the axe, bow and shield in the plan were not possible. The pixel font has no parentheses or middle dot. game.go fades, so tests need settle time. Escape is both pause and cancel. A FlowField keeps its old map after a floor change.',\n    'Built myself: the floor generator with its flood-fill check, the monster and generator rules, the hero rules, and a small list widget for menus (no E.Menu or E.Shell).',\n    'Hardest: finding supported options, such as Humanoid gear and sound preset names, in the API index and the source.',\n    'Engine changes: none. The plan\\'s changes E1 to E8 were not made; each was worked around. See ENGINE-CHANGES.md.',\n    'Would change: one list of valid options for each constructor, and the list of characters the pixel font draws.'\n  ]],\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\n    'Liked most: the run-folder rules, the one-command test rule with failures only, and the done checklist.',\n    'Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md name the title differently (TASK asks for a pick by RNG), and the done condition asks for every feature while the plan is far larger than one session.',\n    'Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and tested rather than the full plan: nine floors, shared-world netcode, a boss and a voice synth.',\n    'Would change: name a must-have slice and say which features the done condition needs, so the rest can be cut openly.'\n  ]]\n];\nconst ABOUT_PAGES = ABOUT_TEXT.map(([title, paras]) => {\n  const lines = [];\n  for (const p of paras) { for (const l of wrapWords(p, 62)) lines.push(l); lines.push(''); }\n  while (lines.length && lines[lines.length - 1] === '') lines.pop();\n  return { title, lines };\n});\nEOF\nnode build.mjs >/dev/null && timeout 200 node tests/shots.mjs ../Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253.html shots 2>&1 | head -2 && timeout 900 node tests/run.mjs 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Write final About text, wrap it, rebuild and rerun the tests"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2785,"cache_read_input_tokens":328405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2785},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"b08f055e-3f7a-4486-9e51-9cac37a287a9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:21:49.557Z","request_id":"req_011Cghsu1cV5DtKPQp95a1SA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YbXM44jPShLi8YiGH5YmBT":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050253__x8ffc89/work/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253 && cat > game/src/80-about.js <<'EOF'\n// About and credits: the pages on the About screen. The Source Information and the feedback sections are the same text\n// as the chat reply and exit-interview.json. Each paragraph is wrapped to the screen when the game loads.\nconst ABOUT_TEXT = [\n  ['CREDITS', [\n    'GAUNTL