{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cght1MQmUwnjDSBqe4DL3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The About page reads cleanly and wraps inside the screen. Now the exit interview and the engine-changes note, then I'll validate the JSON."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1381,"cache_read_input_tokens":342345,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1381},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"0c4f72ed-ba8f-4269-8752-020cf654b826","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:22:35.075Z","request_id":"req_011Cght1M4gZp36NrQaR5H7y"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cght1MQmUwnjDSBqe4DL3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RpToDspjpY88eWqBFaC9Zc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050253__x8ffc89/work/exit-interview.json","content":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:53\",\n    \"source\": \"Gauntlet, Atari Games, 1985 arcade\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, top-down hack-and-shoot\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Three-quarter overhead, with top-down and isometric in Settings\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff, engine unmodified), HTML5 Canvas 2D, Web Audio; tests on Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's PS1-era 2D look: procedural rigs, textured floors and walls, canvas lighting, pixel sprites for items and generators. One realm, The Larder, in this build.\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine rigs and E.MOVES attacks (overhead swing, throw). Monsters and generators bob and flash. No custom animation set.\",\n    \"audio\": \"Engine chip songs (title, adventure, victory) and engine sound presets. No voices and no original music in this build.\",\n    \"online\": \"none\",\n    \"testing\": \"43 headless checks behind one command, a scripted two-hero playthrough of all three floors to the ending run twice with the same result, the engine's browser checker, and screenshots\",\n    \"research\": \"Engine docs (API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md) and engine source; the AI Hub client files were fetched but not used; no web research\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; Chromium through Playwright for the browser checks\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 13 issues. Four were game-breaking: Escape could not open the pause menu, the pause overlay crashed on Resume, the last stairs crashed into a missing floor, and a second run would never show its game over.\",\n    \"Four were game-breaking, as above. The rest were smaller: autopilot stalls on floors after the first, a controller symbol default not applied at boot, overlapping quips on the class select, an over-long Dev Tools page, and characters the pixel font cannot draw.\",\n    \"Most helpful test: the scripted playthrough from title to ending, through every scene, run twice.\",\n    \"Least helpful test: the screenshot look notes, which flagged the flat colours of a dungeon.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Liked most: the TileMap, Humanoid rigs, FlowField and Bullets do the hard parts, and headless advance and input make a whole playthrough run in seconds.\",\n    \"Stuck or guessed wrong: yes. Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, so the axe, bow and shield in the plan were not possible. The pixel font has no middle dot. game.go fades, so tests need settle time. Escape is bound to both pause and cancel. A FlowField keeps its old map after a floor change.\",\n    \"Built myself: the floor generator with its flood-fill check, the monster and generator rules, the hero rules, and a small list widget for menus (no E.Menu or E.Shell).\",\n    \"Hardest: finding supported options, such as Humanoid gear and sound preset names, in the API index and the source.\",\n    \"Engine changes: none. The plan's changes E1 to E8 were not made; each was worked around. See ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\",\n    \"Would change: one list of valid options for each constructor, and the list of characters the pixel font draws.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"Liked most: the run-folder rules, the one-command test rule with failures only, and the done checklist.\",\n    \"Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md name the title differently (TASK asks for a pick by RNG), and the done condition asks for every feature while the plan is far larger than one session.\",\n    \"Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and tested rather than the full plan: nine floors, shared-world netcode, a boss and a voice synth.\",\n    \"Would change: name a must-have slice and say which features the done condition needs, so the rest can be cut openly.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Gauntletdown\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Four fools. One hungry dungeon.\",\n    \"description\": \"A one-to-four player co-op dungeon crawl inspired by Gauntlet: blast hordes, smash generators and eat before your life force runs out. Play together on one screen.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Action\",\n    \"source\": \"Gauntlet\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Move WASD or left stick · Aim mouse or right stick · Fire click, Space or R2 · Magic right-click, Q or △ · Pause Esc or Options\",\n    \"tags\": [\"co-op\", \"arcade\", \"fantasy\", \"comedy\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1381,"cache_read_input_tokens":342345,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1381},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"9bc047fd-48c3-46b6-960b-670c0f797685","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:22:43.822Z","request_id":"req_011Cght1M4gZp36NrQaR5H7y","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RpToDspjpY88eWqBFaC9Zc":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050253__x8ffc89/work/exit-interview.json","content":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:53\",\n    \"source\": \"Gauntlet, Atari Games, 1985 arcade\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, top-down hack-and-shoot\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Three-quarter overhead, with top-down and isometric in Settings\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff, engine unmodified), HTML5 Canvas 2D, Web Audio; tests on Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's PS1-era 2D look: procedural rigs, textured floors and walls, canvas lighting, pixel sprites for items and generators. One realm, The Larder, in this build.\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine rigs and E.MOVES attacks (overhead swing, throw). Monsters and generators bob and flash. No custom animation set.\",\n    \"audio\": \"Engine chip songs (title, adventure, victory) and engine sound presets. No voices and no original music in this build.\",\n    \"online\": \"none\",\n    \"testing\": \"43 headless checks behind one command, a scripted two-hero playthrough of all three floors to the ending run twice with the same result, the engine's browser checker, and screenshots\",\n    \"research\": \"Engine docs (API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md) and engine source; the AI Hub client files were fetched but not used; no web research\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; Chromium through Playwright for the browser checks\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 13 issues. Four were game-breaking: Escape could not open the pause menu, the pause overlay crashed on Resume, the last stairs crashed into a missing floor, and a second run would never show its game over.\",\n    \"Four were game-breaking, as above. The rest were smaller: autopilot stalls on floors after the first, a controller symbol default not applied at boot, overlapping quips on the class select, an over-long Dev Tools page, and characters the pixel font cannot draw.\",\n    \"Most helpful test: the scripted playthrough from title to ending, through every scene, run twice.\",\n    \"Least helpful test: the screenshot look notes, which flagged the flat colours of a dungeon.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Liked most: the TileMap, Humanoid rigs, FlowField and Bullets do the hard parts, and headless advance and input make a whole playthrough run in seconds.\",\n    \"Stuck or guessed wrong: yes. Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, so the axe, bow and shield in the plan were not possible. The pixel font has no middle dot. game.go fades, so tests need settle time. Escape is bound to both pause and cancel. A FlowField keeps its old map after a floor change.\",\n    \"Built myself: the floor generator with its flood-fill check, the monster and generator rules, the hero rules, and a small list widget for menus (no E.Menu or E.Shell).\",\n    \"Hardest: finding supported options, such as Humanoid gear and sound preset names, in the API index and the source.\",\n    \"Engine changes: none. The plan's changes E1 to E8 were not made; each was worked around. See ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\",\n    \"Would change: one list of valid options for each constructor, and the list of characters the pixel font draws.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"Liked most: the run-folder rules, the one-command test rule with failures only, and the done checklist.\",\n    \"Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md name the title differently (TASK asks for a pick by RNG), and the done condition asks for every feature while the plan is far larger than one session.\",\n    \"Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and tested rather than the full plan: nine floors, shared-world netcode, a boss and a voice synth.\",\n    \"Would change: name a must-have slice and say which features the done condition needs, so the rest can be cut openly.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Gauntletdown\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Four fools. One hungry dungeon.\",\n    \"description\": \"A one-to-four player co-op dungeon crawl inspired by Gauntlet: blast hordes, smash generators and eat before your life force runs out. Play together on one screen.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Action\",\n    \"source\": \"Gauntlet\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Move WASD or left stick · Aim mouse or right stick · Fire click, Space or R2 · Magic right-click, Q or △ · Pause Esc or Options\",\n    \"tags\": [\"co-op\", \"arcade\", \"fantasy\", \"comedy\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\n"}}}
