{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cght5Y1bw5nTVUubpvnir","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is built and tested, but it does not meet the goal's done condition. The goal asks for every TASK.md feature, and this build covers a subset. The condition isn't met, so I'm stopping here rather than claiming it.\n\n## What's built\n\n- **Bundle:** `work/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253.html` (single file, opens from `file://`, no external requests).\n- **Dev folder:** `work/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253/`, with source in `game/src/`, the build script, `tests/`, and screenshots in `shots/`.\n- **Exit interview:** `work/exit-interview.json` (parses; every field is filled).\n- **Title:** Gauntletdown, the riff taken from PLAN.md's RNG pick. TASK.md asked for my own pick, so this is a deviation. I followed STAGE.md's \"use the title it gives\".\n\nWorking in this build:\n- Title, class select (four heroes, 1–4 players by pad or keyboard halves), card, play, pause, How to Play, High Scores, Settings, About with the four feedback sections.\n- Three floors generated from seeds, each checked by a flood fill so the stairs are always reachable.\n- Ghosts and gnashers, urn and den generators, food, keys and doors, stairs, life-force drain, continue, game over.\n- Dev Tools in four pages (cheats, warps, gives, tuning steps). Controller symbols switch between PlayStation and Xbox. Attract mode after 10 idle seconds, with any input returning to title. Touch-only notice.\n\n## Not built (the done condition needs these)\n\n- Six of the nine floors, the boss, both treasure rooms, Descent II.\n- AI Hub shared-world sessions. The bundle carries no hub client or session metas.\n- Amulets, special potions, traps, transporters, runes, force fields, spikes, fake walls, cracked walls, and most of the bestiary.\n- Babble voices and original music (only the engine's songs and sound presets are used).\n- The engine changes E1–E8. None were made, and each was worked around.\n\n## Checks run\n\n- `node tests/run.mjs`: 43 checks, 0 failed. Covers floor solvability, the front end, the simulation rules, dev tools, attract, and a scripted two-hero playthrough from title to ending, run twice with the same result.\n- Engine browser checker and screenshots of title, class select, play, pause, Dev Tools and About. No console errors in the final build.\n\nThe checks found about 13 real bugs. Four were game-breaking, and all are fixed.\n\n## Known issues\n\n- **Balance:** a bot with no cheats clears all three floors and finishes with about 1,600 health, so it is far too easy. The Dev Tools tuning steps exist, but I did not tune anything.\n- **Autopilot:** the attract bots are invulnerable, which is by design.\n\n## Choices I made\n\n- Floors are generated from seeds rather than hand-authored, so they are not the plan's layouts.\n- The hub is not integrated. The build makes no session claim, rather than advertising one it can't run.\n- Menus, pause and settings are my own list widget, not `E.Menu` or `E.Shell`.\n- The score table auto-fills initials from the class tag, since there is no letter wheel.\n\n## Required sections\n\n**Source Information:** 2026-11-04 05:02:53. Gauntlet (Atari Games, 1985). Plan: PLAN.md. Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, three-quarter overhead. my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (engine unmodified), Canvas 2D, Web Audio. Engine look, one realm. Engine rigs and attacks. Engine songs and presets, no voices. Online: none. Testing: 43 headless checks, a playthrough run twice, the browser checker. Research: engine docs and source. Environment: Claude Code CLI, Linux, Chromium via Playwright. Model: claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium. Usage: unknown.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** About 13 issues, four game-breaking (Escape could not open pause, pause crashed on Resume, the last stairs crashed, a second run would never show game over). Most helpful: the scripted playthrough to the ending. Least helpful: the screenshot look notes.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** Liked most: TileMap, rigs, FlowField, Bullets, and headless advance. Stuck: Humanoid gear is limited to sword, gun and staff, and the pixel font lacks a middle dot. Built myself: the floor generator, monster and hero rules, the menu widget. Hardest: finding supported options in the API index. Engine changes: none. Would change: one list of valid constructor options.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** Liked most: the run-folder rules, the one-command test rule, and the done checklist. Confusing: the title rule conflicts with the plan's title, and the done condition is far larger than one session. Hardest: keeping scope to what can be finished. Would change: name a must-have slice and say which features the done condition needs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1596,"cache_read_input_tokens":351395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1596},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"100587fa-18c5-4479-982e-8afad5273059","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:23:44.988Z","request_id":"req_011Cght5XhW1Asqdv6iTujnU"}
