{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015hEBXadnno4t25DRkA7oy9","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n25:## Modes\n27:A game declares one mode.\n32:| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n33:| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n44:Games tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n45:`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n49:## A round\n58:5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n62:### Tags\n69:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n77:- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n88:### The client\n94:- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n106:### Joining\n111:- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\n126:| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n127:| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n128:| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n134:### The card\n141:AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n166:choices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\n181:### The start\n188:### Reporting\n190:- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n194:  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n196:- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n204:### Time-up and the end\n207:  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n208:  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n218:| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n222:### Leaving\n226:- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n227:- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n230:  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n233:### Scoring\n235:- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n254:## Sending data between copies\n256:### Parallel\n260:### Ghost\n267:### Shared world\n277:### `send()` and `message`\n294:## Rules\n314:## Test it\n328:The hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n330:`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n339:- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n340:  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n341:- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n358:## Reference\n360:### Tags\n366:| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n372:### API\n377:| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n382:| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n383:| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n384:| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n385:| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n406:### Versions","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"54f7364a-f7c0-4d17-a730-1dd3211d9fce","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:40:19.137Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n25:## Modes\n27:A game declares one mode.\n32:| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n33:| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n44:Games tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\