{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghuv7tGHHCH7G9hFn1pv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X7zYJfcgaqgn2DzSLc6rZP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050253__x8ffc89/work && cat > $D/exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:53\",\n    \"source\": \"Gauntlet, Atari Games, 1985 arcade\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, top-down hack-and-shoot\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Three-quarter overhead, with top-down and isometric in Settings\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff, engine unmodified), HTML5 Canvas 2D, Web Audio; AI Hub client 1.4.0 unmodified; tests on Node 24, Playwright 1.63.0\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's PS1-era 2D look: procedural rigs, textured floors and walls, canvas lighting, pixel sprites for items, generators, traps and the King; three realms and a banquet hall\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine rigs and E.MOVES attacks (overhead swing, throw); bobbing ghosts, lobbed crocks, imp fireballs, the King's phases. No new move sets.\",\n    \"audio\": \"Six original songs with a drum layer, sound effects, and Babble voices (syllable synth) for the narrator and the heroes, all written in code. No audio files.\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub ghost-mode sessions, 1 to 4 players, each on their own copy, reporting a score. No shared-world mode.\",\n    \"testing\": \"59 headless checks behind one command, a scripted playthrough of every stage to the ending run twice with the same result, the hub harness conformance round (16 checks, 2 and 4 players), the engine browser checker, and screenshots\",\n    \"research\": \"Engine docs (API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md), engine source, and the AI Hub README and client; no web research\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; Chromium through Playwright for the browser checks\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 20 issues. Seven were game-breaking: Escape could not open the pause menu, the pause overlay crashed on Resume, the last stairs crashed into a missing floor, a second run would never show its game over, specials, amulets and skip stairs never spawned, a session skipped its own card so nobody could answer Ready, and a touch-only device could start a game.\",\n    \"The other thirteen were smaller: autopilot stalls on floors after the first and at the King's gauntlet, a controller symbol default not applied at boot, overlapping quips on the class select, an over-long Dev Tools page, characters the pixel font cannot draw, a join hint over the fullscreen button, and aim assist and the camera view not applied at start-up.\",\n    \"Most helpful test: the scripted playthrough from title to ending, through every stage, run twice.\",\n    \"Least helpful test: the screenshot look notes, which flagged the flat colours of a dungeon.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Liked most: the TileMap, Humanoid rigs, FlowField and Bullets do the hard parts, and headless advance and input make a whole playthrough run in seconds.\",\n    \"Stuck or guessed wrong: yes. Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, so the axe, bow and shield in the plan were not possible. The pixel font has no middle dot. game.go fades, so tests need settle time. Escape is bound to both pause and cancel. A FlowField keeps its old map after a stage change. The sound voices take only the filters and waves the synth names.\",\n    \"Built myself: the stage generator with its flood-fill check, the monster, hazard and boss rules, the hero rules, the menu widget, the Babble voices, the songs, and the ghost-mode session.\",\n    \"Hardest: finding supported options, such as Humanoid gear and sound preset names, in the API index and the source, and keeping a moving world's state consistent across scenes.\",\n    \"Engine changes: none. The plan's changes E1 to E8 were not made; each was worked around. See ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\",\n    \"Would change: one list of valid options for each constructor, and the list of characters the pixel font draws.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"Liked most: the run-folder rules, the one-command test rule with failures only, and the done checklist.\",\n    \"Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md name the title differently (TASK asks for a pick by RNG), and the done condition asks for every feature while the plan is far larger than one session.\",\n    \"Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and tested rather than the full plan: shared-world netcode, the full bestiary, the boss's full choreography and a voice synth that sounds right by ear.\",\n    \"Would change: name a must-have slice and say which features the done condition needs, so the rest can be cut openly.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Gauntletdown\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Four fools. One hungry dungeon.\",\n    \"description\": \"A one-to-four player co-op dungeon crawl inspired by Gauntlet: blast hordes, smash generators and eat before your life force runs out. Play together on one screen, or race for the top score in AI Hub rounds.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Action\",\n    \"source\": \"Gauntlet\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Move WASD or left stick · Aim mouse or right stick · Fire click, Space or R2 · Magic right-click, Q or △ · Pause Esc or Options\",\n    \"tags\": [\"co-op\", \"arcade\", \"fantasy\", \"comedy\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('$D/exit-interview.json'));print('parses', len(d['testingFeedback']), len(d['engineFeedback']), len(d['promptFeedback']))\"","description":"Rewrite the exit interview to match the current build"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2303,"cache_read_input_tokens":550209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2303},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"098b6d57-9506-4bee-9380-26d9084977f4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:47:48.246Z","request_id":"req_011Cghuv7XgnAhS5AzxTZk2i","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01X7zYJfcgaqgn2DzSLc6rZP":{"command":"D=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050253__x8ffc89/work && cat > $D/exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:53\",\n    \"source\": \"Gauntlet, Atari Games, 1985 arcade\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, top-down hack-and-shoot\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Three-quarter overhead, with top-down and isometric in Settings\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff, engine unmodified), HTML5 Canvas 2D, Web Audio; AI Hub client 1.4.0 unmodified; tests on Node 24, Playwright 1.63.0\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's PS1-era 2D look: procedural rigs, textured floors and walls, canvas lighting, pixel sprites for items, generators, traps and the King; three realms and a banquet hall\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine rigs and E.MOVES attacks (overhead swing, throw); bobbing ghosts, lobbed crocks, imp fireballs, the King's phases. No new move sets.\",\n    \"audio\": \"Six original songs with a drum layer, sound effects, and Babble voices (syllable synth) for the narrator and the heroes, all written in code. No audio files.\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub ghost-mode sessions, 1 to 4 players, each on their own copy, reporting a score. No shared-world mode.\",\n    \"testing\": \"59 headless