{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvZ8j9NEGz4yNbgMCi1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hub scenarios pass on the shared-world build: the standard round, the latency and loss round, host-leave, and the server round with no player of its own. The remaining gaps are the new move sets and the King's fuller choreography, plus the unverified voice quality. I'll update the About text, the exit interview and the engine-changes note to match this build."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_read_input_tokens":608659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1277},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"1fe686d6-6295-40b2-93d3-be136446de38","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:56:01.874Z","request_id":"req_011CghvZ8Kr2qKc3jp5EiwcL"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvZ8j9NEGz4yNbgMCi1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MdUoBmMsR85fFPrt6U24oZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050253__x8ffc89/work && python3 - \"$D\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys,json\nD=sys.argv[1]\nJ=D+'/exit-interview.json'; d=json.load(open(J))\nd['sourceInformation']['online']='AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1 to 4 players: the host copy runs one world, the others send their player\\'s intents and show its snapshots. Passes the hub conformance round (2 and 4 players, latency, loss, host leave, server host).'\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='62 headless checks behind one command (floors, front end, play, dev tools, attract, a scripted playthrough of every stage to the ending run twice, the new mechanics, the letter wheel); the hub harness conformance rounds (standard, latency and loss, host leave, server); the engine browser checker; screenshots'\nd['sourceInformation']['research']='Engine docs (API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md), engine source, and the AI Hub README and client; no web research'\nd['sourceInformation']['audio']='Six original songs with a drum layer for the King, sound effects, and Babble voices (a syllable synth) for the narrator and the heroes, all written in code. No audio files. The voices were not checked by ear.'\nd['sourceInformation']['animation']='Engine rigs and E.MOVES attacks (overhead swing, throw); bobbing ghosts, lobbed crocks, imp fireballs, the King\\'s phases; gear (axe head, shield, bow) drawn on the rigs. No new move sets.'\nd['testingFeedback'][0]='About 22 issues. Eight were game-breaking: Escape could not open the pause menu, the pause overlay crashed on Resume, the last stairs crashed into a missing floor, a second run would never show its game over, specials, amulets and skip stairs never spawned, a session skipped its own card so nobody could answer Ready, a touch-only device could start a game, and the shared world had no client path until the hub harness exposed it.'\nd['testingFeedback'][1]='The other fourteen were smaller: autopilot stalls on floors after the first and at the King\\'s gauntlet, a controller symbol default not applied at boot, overlapping quips on the class select, an over-long Dev Tools page, characters the pixel font cannot draw, a join hint over the fullscreen button, aim assist and the camera view not applied at start-up, and headless saves that silently did nothing.'\nd['engineFeedback'][1]='Stuck or guessed wrong: yes. Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, so the axe, bow and shield were drawn as overlays instead. The pixel font has no middle dot. game.go fades, so tests need settle time. Escape is bound to both pause and cancel. A FlowField keeps its old map after a stage change. The engine\\'s store is empty headless, so the tests supply a memory store. The hub\\'s harness needed unbuffered output from the server.'\nd['promptFeedback'][2]='Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and tested rather than the full plan: the full move sets, the King\\'s complete choreography, and a voice synth that sounds right by ear.'\nd['aiHub']['description']='A one-to-four player co-op dungeon crawl inspired by Gauntlet: blast hordes, smash generators and eat before your life force runs out. Play together on one screen, or in one shared AI Hub world.'\nd['aiHub']['tags']=['co-op', 'arcade', 'fantasy', 'comedy', 'retro']\njson.dump(d, open(J,'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2); open(J,'a').write('\\n')\n# sync the About pages from the JSON\np=D+'/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253/game/src/80-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ndef q(t): return \"'\" + t.replace(\"\\\\\", \"\\\\\\\\\").replace(\"'\", \"\\\\'\") + \"'\"\ndef block(title, items): return \"  ['\"+title+\"', [\\n\" + \",\\n\".join(\"    \"+q(t) for t in items) + \"\\n  ]]\"\nfor title,key in [('TESTING FEEDBACK','testingFeedback'),('ENGINE FEEDBACK','engineFeedback'),('PROMPT FEEDBACK','promptFeedback')]:\n    a=s.index(\"  ['\"+title+\"', [\"); b=s.index(\"\\n  ]]\", a)+len(\"\\n  ]]\")\n    s=s[:a]+block(title,d[key])+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"    'Online: AI Hub ghost-mode sessions, 1 to 4 players, each on their own copy. Testing: 59 headless checks, a scripted playthrough run twice, the hub harness, the engine browser checker. Research: engine docs and source; no web research.',\",\n            \"    'Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1 to 4 players, one world on the host copy. Testing: 62 headless checks, a scripted playthrough run twice, the hub harness, the engine browser checker. Research: engine docs and source; no web research.',\")\ns=s.replace(\"'Engine changes: none, see ENGINE-CHANGES.md.',\",\"'Engine changes: none, see ENGINE-CHANGES.md.',\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\ne=D+'/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253/ENGINE-CHANGES.md'; t=open(e).read()\nt=t.replace(\"| Hub | Shared-world netcode (not an engine change) | Not made. The session runs in ghost mode instead, which the hub README allows |\",\n            \"| Hub | Shared-world netcode (not an engine change) | Built in the game code (61-session.js): the host runs the world, the others send intents, snapshots at eight a second |\")\nopen(e,'w').write(t)\nprint('synced')\nEOF\ncd $D/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253 && node build.mjs >/dev/null && timeout 900 node tests/run.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 && python3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('$D/exit-interview.json'));print('json ok')\"","description":"Update the exit interview, About pages and notes to the shared-world build; rebuild and verify"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_read_input_tokens":608659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1277},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"2bca1d24-131b-4710-8f31-ee83340a225e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:56:09.916Z","request_id":"req_011CghvZ8Kr2qKc3jp5EiwcL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MdUoBmMsR85fFPrt6U24oZ":{"command":"D=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050253__x8ffc89/work && python3 - \"$D\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys,json\nD=sys.argv[1]\nJ=D+'/exit-interview.json'; d=json.load(open(J))\nd['sourceInformation']['online']='AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1 to 4 players: the host copy runs one world, the others send their player\\'s intents and show its snapshots. Passes the hub conformance round (2 and 4 players, latency, loss, host leave, server host).'\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='62 headless checks behind one command (floors, front end, play, dev tools, attract, a scripted playthrough of every stage to the ending run twice, the new mechanics, the letter wheel); the hub harness conformance rounds (standard, latency and loss, host leave, server); the engine browser checker; screenshots'\nd['sourceInformation']['research']='Engine docs (API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md), engine source, and the AI Hub README and client; no web research'\nd['sourceInformation']['audio']='Six original songs with a drum layer for the King, sound effects, and Babble voices (a syllable synth) for the narrator and the heroes, all written in code. No audio files. The voices were not checked by ear.'\nd['sourceInformation']['animation']='Engine rigs and E.MOVES attacks (overhead swing, throw); bobbing ghosts, lobbed crocks, imp fireballs, the King\\'s phases; gear (axe head, shield, bow) drawn on the rigs. No new move sets.'\nd['testingFeedback'][0]='About 22 issues. Eight were game-breaking: Escape could not open the pause menu, the pause overlay crashed on Resume, the last stairs crashed into a missing floor, a second run would never show its game over, specials, amulets and skip stairs never spawned, a session skipped its own card so nobody could answer Ready, a touch-only device could start a game, and the shared world had no client path until the hub harness exposed it.'\nd['testingFeedback'][1]='The other fourteen were smaller: autopilot stalls on floors after the first and at the King\\'s gauntlet, a controller symbol default not applied at boot, overlapping quips on the class select, an over-long Dev Tools page, characters the pixel font cannot draw, a join hint over the fullscreen button, aim assist and the camera view not applied at start-up, and headless saves that silently did nothing.'\nd['engineFeedback'][1]='Stuck or guessed wrong: yes. Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, so the axe, bow and shield were drawn as overlays instead. The pixel font has no middle dot. game.go fades, so tests need settle time. Escape is bound to both pause and cancel. A FlowField keeps its old map after a stage change. The engine\\'s store is empty headless, so the tests supply a memory store. The hub\\'s harness needed unbuffered output from the server.'\nd['promptFeedback'][2]='Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and tested rather than the full plan: the full move sets, the King\\'s complete choreography, and a voice synth that sounds right by ear.'\nd['aiHub']['description']='A one-to-four player co-op dungeon crawl inspired by Gauntlet: blast hordes, smash generators and eat before your life force runs out. Play together on one screen, or in one shared AI Hub world.'\nd['aiHub']['tags']=['co-op', 'arcade', 'fantasy', 'comedy', 'retro']\njson.dump(d, open(J,'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2); open(J,'a').write('\\n')\n# sync the About pages from the JSON\np=D+'/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253/game/src/80-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ndef q(t): return \"'\" + t.replace(\"\\\\\", \"\\\\\\\\\").replace(\"'\", \"\\\\'\") + \"'\"\ndef block(title, items): return \"  ['\"+title+\"', [\\n\" + \",\\n\".join(\"    \"+q(t) for t in items) + \"\\n  ]]\"\nfor title,key in [('TESTING FEEDBACK','testingFeedback'),('ENGINE FEEDBACK','engineFeedback'),('PROMPT FEEDBACK','promptFeedback')]:\n    a=s.index(\"  ['\"+title+\"', [\"); b=s.index(\"\\n  ]]\", a)+len(\"\\n  ]]\")\n    s=s[:a]+block(title,d[key])+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"    'Online: AI Hub ghost-mode sessions, 1 to 4 players, each on their own copy. Testing: 59 headless checks, a scripted playthrough run twice, the hub harness, the engine browser checker. Research: engine docs and source; no web research.',\",\n            \"    'Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1 to 4 players, one world on the host copy. Testing: 62 headless checks, a scripted playthrough run twice, the hub harness, the engine browser checker. Research: engine docs and source; no web research.',\")\ns=s.replace(\"'Engine changes: none, see ENGINE-CHANGES.md.',\",\"'Engine changes: none, see ENGINE-CHANGES.md.',\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\ne=D+'/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253/ENGINE-CHANGES.md'; t=open(e).read()\nt=t.replace(\"| Hub | Shared-world netcode (not an engine change) | Not made. The session runs in ghost mode instead, which the hub README allows |\",\n            \"| Hub | Shared-world netcode (not an engine change) | Built in the game code (61-session.js): the host runs the world, the others send intents, snapshots at eight a second |\")\nopen(e,'w').write(t)\nprint('synced')\nEOF\ncd $D/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253 && node build.mjs >/dev/null && timeout 900 node tests/run.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 && python3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('$D/exit-interview.json'));print('json ok')\"","description":"Update the exit interview, About pages and notes to the shared-world build; rebuild and verify"}}}
