{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvcynkDUNb3yyL1Er8r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The done condition is still not met on a strict reading. Shared-world, the letter wheel, the Dev Tools tools and the gear overlays are now built and tested. What's left is the full move sets, the King's complete choreography, and checking the voices by ear.\n\n## Changed this round\n\n- **Shared-world hub mode:** the host copy runs the whole world. Other copies send their player's intents at 12 a second, and the host sends a snapshot eight times a second, plus a stage message when the descent moves on. The hub's own harness passes 14 of 14 checks in the standard round, with latency and loss, with host-leave, and with the server host (15 of 15 there). Clients show the host's state with smoothing and no prediction, so their own hero lags.\n- **Letter wheel:** qualifying players type their initials on their own controller, with up and down for letters and left and right for slots. Game over and the ending both route through it.\n- **Dev Tools:** bot plays player 1, hitbox overlay, monster-target overlay, and reveal secrets (opens every fake and cracked wall).\n- **Dinner Bell:** passes to a friend who touches the marked hero.\n- **Gear:** the berserker's blade gets an axe head, the shieldmaiden gets a shield, and the ranger gets a bow, all drawn as overlays on the engine's rigs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node tests/run.mjs`: 62 checks, 0 failed.\n- `node tests/hub-browser.mjs` in the four scenarios above: all pass.\n- Engine browser checker: no errors.\n\n## Still missing\n\n- **Move sets:** no new attack or throw animations. The bow draw, the shield bash and the axe swing use the engine's existing moves.\n- **King choreography:** the fight has all three phases, feast denial, waves, charge, fog and defeat, but the scripted staging the plan describes is simplified.\n- **Bestiary depth:** the monsters have the plan's core behaviours, not every detail. The Tithe arrives on the choir only.\n- **Voices and music:** the Babble voices and the six songs are written in code, but I have not listened to them.\n- **Prediction:** clients don't predict their own movement, so the hero lags on slow links.\n- **Engine changes E1–E8:** not made. The plan lists them, but TASK.md doesn't require them.\n\n## Required sections\n\n**Source Information:** 2026-11-04 05:02:53. Gauntlet (Atari Games, 1985). Plan: PLAN.md. Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, three-quarter overhead. my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (engine unmodified) with AI Hub client 1.4.0 unmodified, on Canvas 2D and Web Audio. Engine look with pixel sprites, three realms and a banquet hall. Engine rigs and attacks, gear as overlays, no new move sets. Six original songs and Babble voices, all in code. Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1–4 players. Testing: 62 headless checks, a playthrough run twice, the hub harness conformance rounds, the browser checker. Research: engine docs and source, AI Hub README and client, no web research. Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless), Linux, Chromium via Playwright. Model: claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium. Usage: unknown.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** About 22 issues. Eight were game-breaking, including pause and game-over failures, specials and skip stairs never spawning, a session skipping its own card, touch devices starting a game, and a shared world with no client path. The other fourteen were smaller. Most helpful: the scripted playthrough from title to ending, run twice. Least helpful: the screenshot look notes.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** Liked most: TileMap, rigs, FlowField and Bullets do the hard parts, and headless advance makes a whole playthrough run in seconds. Stuck: Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, so the axe, bow and shield are overlays. The pixel font has no middle dot. The engine's store is empty headless, so the tests supply a memory store. Built myself: the stage generator, the monster and hazard rules, the boss, the Babble voices, the songs, and the shared-world session. Hardest: finding supported options in the API index and source. Engine changes: none; see ENGINE-CHANGES.md. Would change: one list of valid constructor options.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** Liked most: the run-folder rules, the one-command test rule, and the done checklist. Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md name the title differently, and the done condition asks for every feature in a plan far larger than one session. Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and tested, especially the full move sets, the King's full choreography, and a voice synth that sounds right by ear. Would change: name a must-have slice, and say which features the done condition needs.\n\nFiles in `work/`: `Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253.html` (the bundle) and `exit-interview.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":727,"cache_read_input_tokens":613060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":727},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"e706880d-3453-4eb7-9cea-36bb999b022f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:56:56.325Z","request_id":"req_011CghvcyNwnLmSm2CLgPbLD"}
