{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvePmumAhCLA3Eu4QjR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm stopping here, and the goal is not met. I can't finish the remaining items in this session without either overstating the work or making more guesses. The bundle and `exit-interview.json` exist and parse, but that doesn't satisfy \"every feature in TASK.md is implemented.\"\n\n## Still unfinished\n\n- **Move sets:** the bow draw, shield bash and axe swing aren't new animations. The heroes use the engine's existing moves, with gear drawn as overlays.\n- **King Famish:** all three phases, feast denial, gnasher waves, the charge, fog and defeat work, but the scripted staging in the plan (his rise, plate fans and gorging animation) doesn't.\n- **Bestiary:** the monsters have their core behaviours, not every detail of the plan's versions. The Tithe appears only on the choir.\n- **Voices and music:** the Babble voices and six songs are in code, but I haven't listened to them, so their quality is unverified.\n- **Client prediction:** non-host copies draw the host's state without predicting their own movement, so their hero lags on slow links.\n- **Engine changes E1–E8:** not made. The plan asks for them; TASK.md doesn't.\n\n## What is done and checked\n\n- The bundle `Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253.html` is in the run folder. It has nine floors, two treasure rooms, the banquet, Descent II, and the features TASK.md's plan lists, including the new hazards, specials, amulets and letter-wheel initials.\n- AI Hub shared-world sessions pass the hub's conformance round in the standard case, with latency and loss, host-leave, and the server host.\n- `node tests/run.mjs` passes 62 headless checks, including a scripted playthrough of every stage to the ending, run twice.\n\n## Required sections\n\n**Source Information:** 2026-11-04 05:02:53. Gauntlet (Atari Games, 1985). Plan: PLAN.md. Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, three-quarter overhead. my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (unmodified) with AI Hub client 1.4.0 (unmodified). Engine look with pixel sprites, three realms and a banquet hall. Engine rigs and attacks, gear as overlays, no new move sets. Six original songs and Babble voices, unverified by ear. Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1–4 players. Testing: 62 headless checks, a playthrough run twice, the hub harness, the browser checker. Research: engine docs and source, AI Hub README and client; no web research. Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless), Linux, Chromium via Playwright. Model: claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium. Usage: unknown.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** About 22 issues. Eight were game-breaking, including pause and game-over failures, specials and skip stairs never spawning, a session skipping its own card, and touch devices starting a game. The other fourteen were smaller. Most helpful: the scripted playthrough. Least helpful: the screenshot look notes.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** Liked most: TileMap, rigs, FlowField and Bullets do the hard parts, and headless advance makes whole playthroughs fast. Stuck: Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, and the pixel font has no middle dot. Built myself: the stage generator, monster and hazard rules, boss, voices, songs, and the shared-world session. Engine changes: none. Would change: one list of valid constructor options.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** Liked most: the run-folder rules, the one-command test rule, and the done checklist. Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md name the title differently, and the done condition asks for every feature in a plan far larger than one session. Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and verified. Would change: name a must-have slice and say which features the done condition needs.\n\nIf you want me to keep going, the next concrete step is the move sets and the King's full choreography. Those are about a day of animation work, and I'd still need your judgement on whether the voices are good enough."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1993,"cache_read_input_tokens":613787,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1993},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"dc3b68e9-b530-4829-b704-a9cd6769d752","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:57:26.557Z","request_id":"req_011CghvePQbJtN7DRDapJiLL"}
