{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvjYeM3t5yXNXJBycnC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The King now has an intro rise, a kneeling pose while he eats, a death pose, and the glowing ribcage in phase three. The suite passes, 62 of 62. The goal is still not met.\n\n## Still missing\n\n- **New move sets:** no bow-draw, shield-bash or axe-swing animations. The heroes use the engine's existing attacks, and the gear is drawn on top.\n- **King Famish:** the intro rise, the eating pose and the death pose are in. His full scripted staging from the plan (plate fans as animated throws, the gorging sequence, the gauntlet tumbling out) is not.\n- **Bestiary:** the monsters have their core behaviours, not every detail the plan describes. The Tithe appears only on the choir.\n- **Voices and music:** the Babble voices and six songs are in code, but nobody has listened to them. Whether they meet the brief is a judgement only you can make.\n- **Client prediction:** non-host copies draw the host's state and don't predict their own movement, so their hero lags on slow links.\n- **Engine changes E1–E8:** not made. The plan asks for them, but TASK.md doesn't.\n\nJudging the voices and music, and choosing which of the remaining items to build, are yours to decide. Without that, I can't call the goal done.\n\n## What is done and checked\n\n- The bundle `Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253.html` is in the run folder, with nine floors, two treasure rooms, the banquet, Descent II, and the hazards, specials, amulets and letter-wheel initials.\n- Shared-world AI Hub sessions pass the hub's conformance round in four scenarios: standard, latency and loss, host-leave, and the server host.\n- `node tests/run.mjs` passes 62 headless checks, including a scripted playthrough to the ending, run twice.\n\n## Required sections\n\n**Source Information:** 2026-11-04 05:02:53. Gauntlet (Atari Games, 1985). Plan: PLAN.md. Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, three-quarter overhead. my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (unmodified) with AI Hub client 1.4.0 (unmodified). Engine look with pixel sprites, three realms and a banquet hall. Engine rigs and attacks, gear as overlays, no new move sets. Six original songs and Babble voices, unverified by ear. Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1–4 players. Testing: 62 headless checks, a playthrough run twice, the hub harness, the browser checker. Research: engine docs and source, AI Hub README and client; no web research. Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless), Linux, Chromium via Playwright. Model: claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium. Usage: unknown.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** About 22 issues. Eight were game-breaking, including pause and game-over failures, specials and skip stairs never spawning, a session skipping its own card, and touch devices starting a game. The other fourteen were smaller. Most helpful: the scripted playthrough. Least helpful: the screenshot look notes.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** Liked most: TileMap, rigs, FlowField and Bullets do the hard parts, and headless advance makes whole playthroughs fast. Stuck: Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, and the pixel font has no middle dot. Built myself: the stage generator, monster and hazard rules, boss, voices, songs, and the shared-world session. Engine changes: none. Would change: one list of valid constructor options.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** Liked most: the run-folder rules, the one-command test rule, and the done checklist. Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md name the title differently, and the done condition asks for every feature in a plan far larger than one session. Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and verified. Would change: name a must-have slice, and say which features the done condition needs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495,"cache_read_input_tokens":620367,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"195503ab-d1bb-4e86-bf1f-6df48b19d7ad","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:58:25.195Z","request_id":"req_011CghvjYGGnZEjLXDLCa6dA"}
