{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvpeD78Xu5gdtabkMi8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added three game-specific moves. The berserker swings an axe, the shieldmaiden bashes with her shield, and the ranger draws a bow. Each plays through the engine's rig, and the suite and browser check both pass. The goal is still not met, for the reasons below.\n\n## Still missing\n\n- **Animations:** only three new moves exist. Their timing and poses are untested by eye, and the King's and monsters' behaviours still use the engine's existing poses.\n- **King Famish:** the plan's full scripted staging (animated plate throws, the gorging sequence, the gauntlet tumble) is not built. He has an intro rise, eating and death poses, and a phase-three glow.\n- **Bestiary:** the monsters have their core behaviours, not every detail the plan describes. The Tithe appears only on the choir.\n- **Voices and music:** written in code but never listened to. Judging them needs a person.\n- **Client prediction:** non-host copies lag on their own movement.\n- **Engine changes E1–E8:** not made. The plan asks for them; TASK.md does not.\n\nWhat's in place and tested is the bundle, the working game, and the hub sessions. I have no way to finish the staging or judge the audio without you. Tell me whether to keep going on the staging and animation polish, or to treat this as the delivered state.\n\n## Required sections\n\n**Source Information:** 2026-11-04 05:02:53. Gauntlet (Atari Games, 1985). Plan: PLAN.md. Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, three-quarter overhead. my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (unmodified), AI Hub client 1.4.0 (unmodified). Engine look with pixel sprites, three realms and a banquet hall. Engine rigs and attacks plus three game moves (axe swing, shield bash, bow draw). Six original songs and Babble voices, unverified by ear. Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1–4 players. Testing: 62 headless checks, a playthrough run twice, the hub harness, the browser checker. Research: engine docs and source, AI Hub README and client; no web research. Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless), Linux, Chromium via Playwright. Model: claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium. Usage: unknown.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** About 22 issues. Eight were game-breaking, including pause and game-over failures, specials and skip stairs never spawning, a session skipping its own card, and touch devices starting a game. The other fourteen were smaller. Most helpful: the scripted playthrough. Least helpful: the screenshot look notes.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** Liked most: TileMap, rigs, FlowField and Bullets do the hard parts, and headless advance makes whole playthroughs fast. Stuck: Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, and the pixel font has no middle dot. Built myself: the stage generator, monster and hazard rules, boss, voices, songs, the shared-world session, and the three moves. Engine changes: none. Would change: one list of valid constructor options.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** Liked most: the run-folder rules, the one-command test rule, and the done checklist. Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md name the title differently, and the done condition asks for every feature in a plan far larger than one session. Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and verified. Would change: name a must-have slice, and say which features the done condition needs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2265,"cache_read_input_tokens":625731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2265},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"f82ecc04-20e5-4445-9408-0f9f18e3e36c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:59:3