{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvvEFNfG71ye1ZVyN7u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Tithe now arrives at two minutes on every floor from floor 5 on, when none is present. The suite still passes, 62 of 62. The goal is still not met.\n\nWhat's left against TASK.md and the plan: King Famish's full scripted staging, the rest of the bestiary detail, client prediction, engine changes E1–E8, and checking the animations, voices and music by eye and ear. I can't finish those responsibly in this session, and the last two need a person to judge them. Please tell me whether you want those built as required or whether this is the delivered state.\n\nThe bundle `Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050253.html` and `exit-interview.json` are in the run folder.\n\n## Required sections\n\n**Source Information:** 2026-11-04 05:02:53. Gauntlet (Atari Games, 1985). Plan: PLAN.md. Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, three-quarter overhead. my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (unmodified), AI Hub client 1.4.0 (unmodified). Engine look with pixel sprites, three realms and a banquet hall. Engine rigs and attacks plus three game moves. Six original songs and Babble voices, unverified by ear. Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions, 1–4 players. Testing: 62 headless checks, a playthrough run twice, the hub harness, the browser checker. Research: engine docs and source, AI Hub README and client; no web research. Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless), Linux, Chromium via Playwright. Model: claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium. Usage: unknown.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** About 22 issues. Eight were game-breaking: pause and game-over failures, specials and skip stairs never spawning, a session skipping its own card, and touch devices starting a game. The other fourteen were smaller. Most helpful: the scripted playthrough. Least helpful: the screenshot look notes.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** Liked most: TileMap, rigs, FlowField and Bullets, and headless advance makes whole playthroughs fast. Stuck: Humanoid weapons are sword, gun and staff only, and the pixel font has no middle dot. Built myself: the stage generator, monster and hazard rules, boss, voices, songs, the shared-world session, and the three moves. Engine changes: none. Would change: one list of valid constructor options.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** Liked most: the run-folder rules, the one-command test rule, and the done checklist. Confusing: PLAN.md and TASK.md name the title differently, and the done condition asks for every feature in a plan far larger than one session. Hardest: keeping to what can be finished and verified. Would change: name a must-have slice, and say which features the done condition needs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1267,"cache_read_input_tokens":633852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1267},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e08c15-1510-4ccd-89c0-2fe447fbc059","uuid":"71e286bb-b714-4b71-b2ba-52670b2ba1fe","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:00:47.997Z","request_id":"req_011CghvvDkN4fjWiJxUHiGLE"}
